{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CrystalIsospinDegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CrystalIsospinDegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_T_helium3_degeneracy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_T_helium3_degeneracy","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L223-L249","doc":"**Corollary (T--³He crystal degeneracy, legacy convention).**\n\nUnder `[CrystalEigenlineSignBlind R]`, two atomic braid words that\ndiffer only by signed-generator inversions at a finite set\nof positions have the same crystal character.  Specialised\nto the legacy disjoint-product words\n\n  `w_T   = σ_1 σ_2 σ_1⁻¹ σ_4 σ_5⁻¹ σ_4   σ_7 σ_8⁻¹ σ_7`\n  `w_He3 = σ_1 σ_2 σ_1⁻¹ σ_4 σ_5   σ_4⁻¹ σ_7 σ_8⁻¹ σ_7`\n\nthey differ at positions 5 and 6 (zero-based indices 4 and 5)\nby paired inversions of `σ_5 ↔ σ_5⁻¹` and `σ_4 ↔ σ_4⁻¹`.\nTherefore `S_crystal(T) = S_crystal(³He)`.\n\nWitness:\n`computations/term7-alpha5-crystal-derivation.witness.json`\nrecords both at 50 dps as `0.0020612874779541296`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_isospin_degeneracy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_isospin_degeneracy","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L201-L221","doc":"**Theorem (crystal isospin degeneracy).**\n\nConditional on `[CrystalEigenlineSignBlind R]`, the crystal character\n`eigWord` is invariant under sign-inversion of any subset of\nthe letters of the word.  Concretely, for any predicate\n`flip : ℕ → Bool`,\n\n  `eigWord (flipAt flip w) = eigWord w`.\n\nProof: instance of `crystal_isospin_degeneracy_aux` at\n`offset = 0`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:crystal-isospin-degeneracy","label":"prop:crystal-isospin-degeneracy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_isospin_degeneracy_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crystal_isospin_degeneracy_aux","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L179-L199","doc":"**Auxiliary lemma (depth-shifted invariance).**\n\nConditional on `[CrystalEigenlineSignBlind R]`, the crystal character of\n`flipAux flip offset w` equals the crystal character of `w` for\nevery offset `offset : ℕ`.  Proof: induction on `w`, using\n`eigLetter_flipAt` on the head and `eigWord_cons` to factor\nthe per-letter contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_flipAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_flipAt","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L168-L175","doc":"A flipped letter under any predicate has the same crystal\ncharacter as the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_invert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_invert","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L155-L166","doc":"A flipped letter has the same crystal character as the\noriginal.  Direct consequence of `eigLetter_sign_blind`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L147-L147","doc":"Per-eigenline multiplicativity: applying generators in\nsequence multiplies their eigenvalues on the same SYT line.\n*Note*: this is multiplicativity of *eigenvalues on a fixed\nSYT line*, not of the irreducible character `χ^λ` (which is\na trace = sum over SYTs and is **not** multiplicative as a\nfunction of the braid word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_sign_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter_sign_blind","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The conjectural input: on every SYT eigenline, σ and σ⁻¹\nhave the same q=0 eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord_nil","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The empty-word eigenvalue product is the multiplicative\nidentity.  Without this axiom `eigWord _ = 0` would\nvacuously satisfy `eigWord_cons`, making the proposition\ntrivially provable for the wrong reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigWord","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L129-L129","doc":"Per-eigenline eigenvalue product along a word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.eigLetter","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L127-L127","doc":"Per-eigenline eigenvalue of a single signed letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalEigenlineSignBlind","kind":"class","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L96-L149","doc":"**Conjectural class.**  A `CrystalEigenlineSignBlind R` instance\nencodes the **per-SYT-eigenline** action of a single signed\nHecke letter at the crystal limit `q = 0`.\n\nFor a fixed standard Young tableau `T` of shape `λ`, the\ncrystal-limit Hecke generator `σ_i` acts diagonally on the\nSYT-basis eigenline through `T` with eigenvalue\n`eigLetter (.pos i) ∈ R`.  The product of these per-letter\neigenvalues along a braid word `w` is `eigWord w ∈ R` — the\n*eigenvalue product on the line through `T`*, **not** the\nfull irreducible character `χ^λ`, which is the *trace*\n\n  `χ^λ(w) = ∑_{T ∈ SYT(λ)} (eigWord w on the line through T)`.\n\nThe full character is therefore a *sum* of `eigWord` values\nover a finite SYT-basis; multiplicativity holds *per\neigenline*, not on the trace.\n\nThe conjectural content (per `conj:crystal-graph-realization`):\non every SYT eigenline, the q→0 actions of `σ_i` and\n`σ_i⁻¹` agree.  This is implemented by the `abs(i)` reduction\nin `term7_alpha5_crystal_derivation.py`.\n\nScope (2026-11-16): this field is a modelling choice, not a\nconsequence of the Hecke relation `(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`, which\ncannot be specialised at `q = 0`.  In `H_n(q)` the eigenvalues of\n`σ_i` are `q, -q⁻¹` and those of `σ_i⁻¹` are `q⁻¹, -q`.  The\nimplication `CrystalGraphRealization ⟹ CrystalEigenlineSignBlind`\nnamed in the module docstring is not proved anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord.flipAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord.flipAt","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L91-L94","doc":"Top-level word-flipping operation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord.flipAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord.flipAux","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L76-L89","doc":"Invert a chosen subset of the letters of a word (specified by\na predicate on positions).  Letters with index `k` such that\n`flip k = true` are inverted; others are unchanged.  Implemented\nvia a recursive helper `flipAux` rather than `List.mapIdx` so\nthe induction step in `crystal_isospin_degeneracy` proceeds by\npattern-matching without reasoning about `mapIdx`'s internal\ncounter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedBraidWord","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L73-L74","doc":"A signed braid word is a list of signed letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.idx_invert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.idx_invert","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L69-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.invert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.invert","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L64-L67","doc":"Inversion of a signed letter swaps `pos ↔ neg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.idx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.idx","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L59-L62","doc":"The generator index of a signed letter (the `|i|` of `σ_i^±`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprSignedLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprSignedLetter","kind":"instance","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprSignedLetter.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprSignedLetter.repr","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqSignedLetter.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqSignedLetter.decEq","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqSignedLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqSignedLetter","kind":"instance","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.neg","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter.pos","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SignedLetter","kind":"inductive","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-isospin-degeneracy.lean#L52-L57","doc":"**A signed braid letter.**  Either `+i` (positive crossing\n`σ_i`, `pos`) or `-i` (negative crossing `σ_i⁻¹`, `neg`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}